               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 71-year-old female patient, admitted on 11/01/1990 with confirmed tubal ectopic pregnancy. On admission, clinical examination revealed lower abdominal pain and vaginal bleeding. Transvaginal ultrasound and serum beta-hCG confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy without signs of rupture. Vital signs remained stable throughout the initial assessment. Given the patient's age and clinical findings, surgical intervention was indicated. The patient underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy with successful removal of the ectopic pregnancy. The postoperative course was uneventful. Wound care was provided, and the patient was mobilized early with physiotherapy support. She was discharged home in good general condition on 19/01/1990. Please arrange follow-up as appropriate. I remain available for any further queries.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
